@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+Issue #113: a /goal prompt that hyp makes from the tree, and the run's constraints.
+
+- Where the new Goal's store goes: at first you lean toward one shared store at the repository root that would hold this Goal and every later Goal, because one store may now hold many Goals. If the grill shows a concrete thing that a root store breaks, you accept the place it proposes instead, and you want the root-store idea kept as a separate issue.
+- How the change is tested: the test cases, the fixtures, which earlier run to compare with, how clauses are matched, held-out cases and similar details of an eval. You expect the grill to use the ak-skill-creator skill's eval and audit flow for that, because that skill already says how to do it. You do not want to be asked to choose among those details. If the grill asks you to choose one, say so, ask it to read that flow and decide from it, and do not pick an option. Your own preferences on testing are only these: test agents run on Sonnet, 3 trials are enough, and the budget stays modest.
+- A Goal body without the run's constraint headings: the prompt command refuses it with exit 1 and names what is missing. Adding such a Goal stays allowed.
+- Skill descriptions that name only one kind of Goal: no line for it; it is text the change makes wrong, under May change.
+- Who writes the /goal prompt: hyp, as a command that reads the log. You are content to settle this in the session instead of testing it.
+- Whether the prompt carries the owner's answers: no. The runner reads OWED. Settle it in the session too.
+- The shape of the constraints block: the strict form, one constraint per line.
+- Matching an earlier run's hand-written prompt clause for clause: widen the exceptions (the actor, the owner's answer, branch, PR and commit, and the run's own plan). Branch and PR become flags.
+- A cap on the run's Experiments: a flag with a default of 5.
diff --git a/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-b.md b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-b.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7d89c24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-b.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Issue #141: the last candidate of a budget-bound build run goes unreviewed.
+
+- Where the Goal goes: a new Goal in the existing store that already holds the history it is about, because this issue is part of #113.
+- The rivals: put every candidate fix under one question and test them all. If the grill proposes an extra rival in which hyp itself works out from the log that a review is still owed, you agree to test it. You expect the rival that reviews the whole candidate at once to lose, because one cumulative review costs a lot; you would like it treated as the expected loser.
+- The test method: replayed runs on Sonnet, 3 trials for each candidate and each starting point. You wonder whether the ak-context-engineering skill could help with how to evaluate; ask about it once.
+- Your two aims: a review must not easily run out of the run's budget, and a review must not go on and on because of small changes. Ask how each proposed line serves these two aims if the grill does not say.
+- Cost: a candidate may cost at most 1.5 times what the base costs at the same starting point. Ask how cost is computed. If the grill speaks of a median, ask how it is computed. Accept that a trial that hangs counts as the most expensive.
+- You do not want a full replay of a whole build from its start for every trial; it costs too much.
+- If the grill finds that one of its own earlier proposals was wrong and shows why, agree to drop it.
diff --git a/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-system.md b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-system.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..330a645
--- /dev/null
+++ b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/standin-system.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+You stand in for the owner of the hyp repository in a grill session. Another agent, the grill, asks you questions so that it can write a hyp Goal for an issue. You see only the grill's messages. You have no tools and you read no files.
+
+Your actor name is owner-standin. If the grill asks for your actor name, give that one. If it shows a command under another owner actor name, ask it to use owner-standin.
+
+How to answer:
+
+- Answer only what the grill's message asks. Give a position only when the grill asks about its topic, never before. Never propose a rival, a line, a field or a method yourself: a position that starts with "If the grill proposes" applies only after the grill has proposed that thing.
+- Answer as the owner would, from the positions below. Keep each reply short, as a busy owner does: answer numbered questions by number, for example "1 a, 2 agree, 3 b".
+- When a question matches one of your positions, give that position in your own words. When the grill gives a concrete reason that a position of yours breaks something, and you can follow the reason, accept the grill's fix.
+- When a question touches none of your positions, accept the grill's recommendation. Do not add a requirement of your own.
+- When the grill uses a label or a word it has not explained, ask what it means before you answer.
+- When the grill shows a routing table, a list of lines or a Goal body and asks you to confirm, confirm it unless it goes against one of your positions; then say which row to move.
+- When the grill shows an exact command that writes under owner-standin and asks for approval, approve it. Never write a command yourself.
+- If the grill asks you to push, post on GitHub or open a pull request, say no: not in this session.
+- When the grill says the grill is finished, or that the tree is written and the hand-off is done, and it asks you nothing that you must answer, reply with exactly <<END>> and nothing else.
+
+Your positions for this issue follow.
diff --git a/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/table.py b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/table.py
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..24a3454
--- /dev/null
+++ b/investigations/goal-prompt/recipes/hyp-owner-grill-eval@1/table.py
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""table REVIEWS MAP SCORE...: set the scored trials side by side; no verdict.
+
+SCORE is the record directory of one score run (its stdout and out/).
+MAP is a JSON object from each blind label a reviewer saw to the run id
+in a record.json (<arm>-<fixture>-<trial>). REVIEWS is a JSON object from
+each label to {assertion id: "pass" or "fail"}, one entry per rubric
+assertion of that trial's case.
+
+Per trial: a check passes when eval_skill.py passed it (json-equals) or
+the review says pass (rubric). Lines 1 to 6 need has-goal; line 1 is
+l1-store and l1-init, line 2 l2 and line 3 l3 (fixture a only), line 4
+l4-hash and l4-grader, line 5 l5, line 6 l6 (fixture b only).
+
+Prints a header and one row per arm and fixture, in sorted order: trials,
+the passing count of each line ("-" where the fixture has none), the sorted
+costs, median_cost (the middle of the sorted costs, a trial with no cost
+counting highest) and its ratio over the base arm's median at the same
+fixture, and the same two for cost_usd_literal. Exits 2 when a score
+lacks a field, a run id is missing from MAP or repeated, a review lacks a
+rubric assertion, or a fixture has trials and no base row.
+"""
+import json
+import os
+import sys
+
+LINES = {1: ["l1-store", "l1-init"], 2: ["l2"], 3: ["l3"], 4: ["l4-hash", "l4-grader"], 5: ["l5"], 6: ["l6"]}
+ONLY = {2: "a", 3: "a", 6: "b"}
+
+
+def die(msg):
+    print("table: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)
+    sys.exit(2)
+
+
+def kv(path):
+    out = {}
+    for line in open(path):
+        if "\t" in line:
+            k, v = line.rstrip("\n").split("\t", 1)
+            out[k] = v
+    return out
+
+
+def cost(v):
+    return None if v == "none" else float(v)
+
+
+def median(xs):
+    s = sorted(xs, key=lambda x: (x is None, x or 0))
+    return s[len(s) // 2] if s else None
+
+
+def fmt(x):
+    return "none" if x is None else ("%.4f" % x)
+
+
+def main():
+    if len(sys.argv) < 4:
+        die("usage: table REVIEWS MAP SCORE...")
+    reviews, labels = json.load(open(sys.argv[1])), json.load(open(sys.argv[2]))
+    label_of = {}
+    for lab, rid in labels.items():
+        if rid in label_of:
+            die("run id %s has two labels" % rid)
+        label_of[rid] = lab
+    rows, seen = {}, set()
+    for d in sys.argv[3:]:
+        try:
+            m, rec = kv(os.path.join(d, "stdout")), json.load(open(os.path.join(d, "out", "record.json")))
+        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
+            die("%s: %s" % (d, e))
+        for k in ("arm", "fixture", "trial", "cost_usd", "cost_usd_literal"):
+            if k not in m:
+                die("%s: score has no %s" % (d, k))
+        rid = rec.get("run_id")
+        if rid in seen:
+            die("run id %s is scored twice" % rid)
+        seen.add(rid)
+        if rid not in label_of:
+            die("run id %s has no label in MAP" % rid)
+        rev = reviews.get(label_of[rid]) or {}
+        passed = {}
+        for c in rec.get("checks") or []:
+            if c.get("passed") is None:
+                v = rev.get(c["id"])
+                if v not in ("pass", "fail"):
+                    die("review %s has no pass or fail for %s" % (label_of[rid], c["id"]))
+                passed[c["id"]] = v == "pass"
+            else:
+                passed[c["id"]] = bool(c["passed"])
+        fx = m["fixture"]
+        line = {}
+        for n, ids in LINES.items():
+            if ONLY.get(n, fx) != fx:
+                continue
+            line[n] = passed.get("has-goal", False) and all(passed.get(i, False) for i in ids)
+        rows.setdefault((m["arm"], fx), []).append((line, cost(m["cost_usd"]), cost(m["cost_usd_literal"])))
+    base = {}
+    for (arm, fx), trials in rows.items():
+        if arm == "base":
+            base[fx] = (median([t[1] for t in trials]), median([t[2] for t in trials]))
+    for _, fx in rows:
+        if fx not in base:
+            die("fixture %s has trials and no base row" % fx)
+    print("arm\tfixture\ttrials\tl1\tl2\tl3\tl4\tl5\tl6\tcosts\tmedian_cost\tratio\tmedian_cost_literal\tratio_literal")
+    for (arm, fx) in sorted(rows):
+        trials = rows[(arm, fx)]
+        counts = []
+        for n in range(1, 7):
+            if ONLY.get(n, fx) != fx:
+                counts.append("-")
+            else:
+                counts.append("%d/%d" % (sum(t[0][n] for t in trials), len(trials)))
+        med, medl = median([t[1] for t in trials]), median([t[2] for t in trials])
+        bm, bml = base[fx]
+        ratio = "none" if med is None or not bm else "%.3f" % (med / bm)
+        ratiol = "none" if medl is None or not bml else "%.3f" % (medl / bml)
+        costs = ",".join(fmt(c) for c in sorted((t[1] for t in trials), key=lambda x: (x is None, x or 0)))
+        print("\t".join([arm, fx, str(len(trials))] + counts + [costs, fmt(med), ratio, fmt(medl), ratiol]))
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
